## Context
A trustworthy statistical table must express uncertainty. Models should
say "I don't know" rather than hallucinate, and aggregates should carry
confidence intervals.

## Actions
1. "I don't know" detection and scoring in extraction
2. Confidence interval estimation on capacity aggregates
3. Add confidence metrics to RunRecord.result_summary

## Exit criteria
- "I don't know" responses detected and scored
- Confidence intervals computed for aggregate statistics
- Metrics visible in measurements table
